title: Pizza Night
---
# Making Beautfiul Food
Making food is as acient as hunanity itself. Our primate ancestors scavenged for food among the various flora and hunted various fauna. Some say that humanity didn't start until we started cooking our food. Cooking was instrumental to human evolution as I learned from Bret Weinstein's and Heather Heying's book, "A Hunter-Gather's Guide to the 21st Century". They spoke that it made food safer, reduced spoilage, detoxified some plants, and increased the calories humans could extract from food. How incredible!

Cooking is instrumental to our existance. It also feeds our higher spirits. Bret and Heather also talk about sharing food around a camp fire in their book. The expeirence of sharing a meal with someone else is improtant. Its an act of giving, care, and openess. That has followed us into the modern world. Sharing a meal is incredible experince. From a simple dinner party to an extravagent feast, the sharing of food is transcendant. 

Those who make their own food must be proud. An ancient skill of turning raw ingrediants into a dance of flavors. Each item added in balance to achieve a perfect blend that elevates the senses. It seems so simple and yet hard to master. Folliwng a recipe simplies the work. The balance already achieved. Yet, so few young americans can achieve this. I know many who can't cook. Relying on simple dishes, ordering out, or prepared items. We must not become that. We must live to cook delicious foods and serve them to ourselves and others. 

That is why making your own pizza is transcendental. 

# Making Pizza
For The American Homebrewer's Association's August 1st Home Fermentation Day, my lovely Fiance and I made home-fermented [sourdough pizza dough](https://homebrewersassociation.org/beyond-beer/how-to-make-sourdough-pizza-dough/) We made a few delicous pies.

![Sourdough Pizza Dough](/assets/images/puffy_dought.jpg)

![Hawaiian Pizza](/assets/images/hawaiian.jpg)

Cooking is so easy to do. A quick skill to aquire that makes your and everyone else satsiated and happy. For every Gen-X'er that I've met that can't cook, they tend to be miserable and unequiped for life.

Eat good food!
